    question: 'What is a frequency response analysis (FRA) test on a transformer?',
    quick: 'Sweep frequency response analysis (SFRA) measures the transformer winding impedance (or transfer function) over a wide frequency band and compares the response to a baseline or to factory data. Changes in the response indicate deformation, displacement or core movement from short-circuit or transport forces. It is a sensitive diagnostic for mechanical integrity.',
