    quick: 'FAT (Factory Acceptance Test) happens at the manufacturer to prove the unit meets the spec before shipment; SAT (Site Acceptance Test) happens after installation to confirm it is set up correctly and ready to energise. FAT covers routine/type tests and inspection; SAT covers commissioning checks, protection, connections and a successful energisation.',
