    quick: 'A three-phase transformer has three windings and delivers three-phase power, used for most industrial and grid applications. A single-phase transformer has one winding pair and is used for single-phase distribution, household supply, reference units and some special loads. Three-phase can be one unit, or three single-phase units banked together.',
    sections: [
      ['Three-phase', 'One unit (or a three-unit bank) converts three-phase power with a more compact, economical core. It supplies motors, industrial plants and the grid.'],
      ['Single-phase', 'One winding pair steps a single-phase supply (e.g. to 230/400 V for households or light commercial). Used for distribution, single-phase loads and reference applications.'],
      ['Banking single-phase units', 'Three single-phase units can be connected (banked) to form a three-phase transformer, useful for spares and for very large units where transporting a single three-phase unit is impractical.'],
    ],
    refs: ['IEC 60076-1', 'IEEE C57.12.00'],
