    title: 'What Insulating Liquids Are Used in Transformers?',
    question: 'What types of insulating liquid are used in a transformer?',
    quick: 'The main insulating liquids are mineral oil (the standard, cost-effective choice), natural esters (biodegradable, high fire point, from vegetable oils), and synthetic esters (high fire point, often for transformers and flame-retardant applications). Silicone oil is used for a few fire-critical designs. Each has a different fire point, environmental profile, cost and compatibility.',
