    title: 'How Is a Transformer Cooling System Maintained?',
    question: 'How is a transformer cooling system maintained?',
    quick: 'Maintain the cooling system by cleaning the radiators and coolers (blocked fin/airways reduce cooling), checking and greasing the fans and their motors, ensuring the oil pumps run and the oil flows, and verifying the temperature control, thermostats and, for OFAF, the oil and air flow. A dirty or failed cooling system rapidly reduces the rating and risks overheating.',
