    quick: 'A winding is formed by winding the insulated conductor on a former (mandrel) in layers or discs, with the correct tension, the spacing and the insulation, so the turns are even and the winding is tight. After winding, it is clamped, the shape held by the insulation and the spacers, and dried and impregnated. The winding geometry and the clamping determine the insulation and the short-circuit strength.',
