    quick: 'A transformer tank ruptures when the internal pressure rises faster than the pressure-relief device can handle — usually from a violent internal arcing fault (a short), a severe overpressure, or a blocked/failing relief. The gas generated by the fault, with the oil, raises the pressure. A massive rupture can be catastrophic, so the protection, the relief, the corrosion and the defect must be managed to prevent it.',
